{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-339540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are first-order linear systems of ODEs?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t)\\,{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+\\sqrt{3}\\,t\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}){x}_{1}(t)+{13}^{2}{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=9{x}_{1}(t)-\\pi {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}^{2}(t)+{x}_{2}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is a first-order linear system of ODEs since it can be written in the standard form, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t), &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0, \\\\ c(t)=2, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=\\sqrt{3}\\,t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is a first-order linear system of ODEs since it can be written in the standard form, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}), &  & b(t)={13}^{2}, &  & f(t)=0, \\\\ c(t)=9, &  & d(t)=-\\pi , &  & g(t)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is not a first-order linear system of ODEs since it contains the terms ${x}_{1}^{2}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}^{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are first-order linear systems of ODEs?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_