"$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2t\\,{x}_{1}(t)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+5{x}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2t\\,{x}_{1}(t)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+5{x}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2t\\,{x}_{1}(t)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,{x}_{2}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2t & 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339645" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339645" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339645" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339645" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\