" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339645" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339645" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the following system of differential equations is written in the form ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then what is the matrix $A?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+5{x}_{1}(t)-9{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+5{x}_{1}(t)-9{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the following system of differential equations is written in the form ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then what is the matrix $A?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)+3{x}_{1}(t)-5{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)-{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)+3{x}_{1}(t)-5{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)-{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-5{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+t\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)\\end{aligned}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of the form\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f≡0$ and $g≡0$ (i.e., both $f$ and $g$ are zero functions), then the system is *homogeneous*. Otherwise, if at least one of $f$ or $g$ is not identically zero, the system is *inhomogeneous*.\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-2, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=4, &  & d(t)=-1, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=1, &  & b(t)=2, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=0, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In matrix form, the system\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=A(t)x(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nis *homogeneous* when $f≡0,$ and *inhomogeneous* when $f≢0.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\n- System II is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/