ttribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In matrix form, the system\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=A(t)x(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nis *homogeneous* when $f≡0,$ and *inhomogeneous* when $f≢0.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since $f=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]≢0.$\n\n- System III is inhomogeneous since $f=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]≢0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+1\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+{e}^{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)+3t\\end{aligned}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of the form\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f≡0$ and $g≡0$ (i.e., both $f$ and $g$ are zero functions), then the system is *homogeneous*. Otherwise, if at least one of $f$ or $g$ is not identically zero, the system is *inhomogeneous*.\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≢0$ and $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=3, &  & b(t)=2, &  & f(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t) \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=4, &  & g(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-1, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=5, &  & d(t)=6, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≢0$ and $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=4, &  & b(t)=0, &  & f(t)={e}^{2} \\\\ c(t)=0, &  & d(t)=1, &  & g(t)=3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339672" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339672" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339672" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)+2{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)+4{e}^{t} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-4{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5){x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of the form\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f≡0$ and $g≡0$ (i.e., both $f$ and $g$ are zero functions), then the system is *homogeneous*. Otherwise, if at least one of $f$ or $g$ is not identically zero, the system is *inhomogeneous*.\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≢0$ and $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-3, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6t) \\\\ c(t)=1, &  & d(t)=-2, &  & g(t)=2{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=1, &  & b(t)=3, &  & f(t)=4{e}^{t} \\\\ c(t)=1, &  & d(t)=-1, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-4, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=1, &  & d(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5), &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t).$ Which of the following vectors are solutions to this equation?\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 5t\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2} \\\\ 2t-8\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we need to substitute each vector into the given matrix differential equation and check if it results in a true statement.\n\nFor ${x}_{1}(t)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}(t)^{′} \\\\ (5t)^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 5t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & \\ne [\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 5t\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for ${x}_{2}(t)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{(2{t}^{2})}^{′} \\\\ {(2t-8)}^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2} \\\\ 2t-8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & \\ne [\\begin{aligned}4{t}^{2} \\\\ 2t-8\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for ${x}_{3}(t)$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{({e}^{2t})}^{′} \\\\ {({e}^{t})}^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"${x}_{3}(t)$ only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${x}_{1}(t)$ only"] ["text" "${x}_{2}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)$ only"] ["text" "${x}_{2}(t)$ only"] ["text" "${x}_{3}(t)$ only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${x}_{3}(t)$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t).$ Which of the following vectors are solutions to this equation?\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}(t)=[\\begin{a