}[\\begin{aligned}({e}^{t})^{′} \\\\ (0)^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & \\ne [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for ${x}_{3}(t)$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}(0)^{′} \\\\ ({e}^{t})^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] & \\ne [\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"${x}_{1}(t)$ only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file_sha256" "3692dc8c27171e38a5aeee563b18dab9e64a5dab13547a09267fe8c91df3ac97"} {"question" "q-339734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7302b1441d4244cdbaf9460cd6041a68c291e99088dd51245ac0d76f5f0d0c0"} {"question" "q-339734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037202/state.json" "file